# Corrections and lessons now made permanent

The package explicitly preserves the lessons that emerged through your pushback:

- **Tailored résumés are not rewrites.** The next chat is directed to preserve 85–90% of an approved baseline and change only 10–15% at the edges. fileciteturn179file5L188-L190
- **Context must precede infrastructure and KPIs.** An unexplained “SQL/Teradata architecture” statement is not acceptable; the business or control problem must come first. The CPI analytical system and dashboard evidence should lead when relevant. fileciteturn179file2L68-L74
- **Every employer requires a job description.** The Census Bureau context may never be omitted simply to make space for additional bullets. fileciteturn179file0L25-L27
- **Leadership must be described accurately.** Your record is operational, technical, mentoring, matrix, governance, and executive-decision leadership—not formal performance-review management. fileciteturn179file7L251-L257
- **The 20M+ figure is an evaluation population, not a 20-million-account correction.** Most accounts required no update; the analysis isolated the smaller targeted-redress population. CPI must also remain prominent rather than being buried behind secondary evidence. fileciteturn180file6L147-L169
- **Power BI and portfolio work remain accurately bounded.** Power BI is a completed public portfolio capability; professional experience includes Tableau and CPI dashboard-data enablement rather than enterprise Power BI administration. fileciteturn180file9L265-L267
- **The merchant-financing project strengthens the résumé selectively.** Its value is the governed architecture, operating intelligence, cash-flow, risk, unit-economics, contract, and acceptance chain. Module 2 offer decisioning is authorized but not represented as complete. fileciteturn180file3L59-L61

